cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the frozen reproducibility artifacts, please cite this repository. A persistent archival DOI is pending and will be added when the deposit is completed."
title: "Reconstruction is not decision identifiability: an exact collision for one-shot communication"
abstract: >-
  Scientific software and frozen reproducibility artifacts accompanying a study of the
  separation between model reconstructability, exact decision identifiability and local
  decision stability in one-shot communicated summaries. The repository contains the
  frozen protocol chain for Phases 0-5, feature-bank and pair manifests, every gate
  summary, and a prospectively frozen cross-mechanism falsification study (CMR-V1) whose
  terminal decision was CMR-D with protocol stop; the later stages of that study were
  never run. Raw third-party datasets, downloaded archives, local feature banks and
  pretrained model weights are not redistributed.
